SUMMARY:Another Opportunity to Learn New Skills - Trekker Training
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\n**TREKKER TRAINING ZOOM CALL*
 *\n**Time: May 6\, 2026 07:30 PM Eastern Time (US and Canada)**\n**Join Zo
 om Meeting**\n**https://us05web.zoom.us/j/9225736911?pwd=QW5DamFQV0c5VDJjS
 is0eGxQZEk4QT09&omn=83784215428**\n**Meeting ID: 922 573 6911**\n**Passcod
 e: crCjL3**\n**Join instructions**\n**https://us05web.zoom.us/meetings/837
 84215428/invitations?signature=npN-GZlfXeunKJDcZIGPTzxQYFGscQsiTXluI1_ydKc
 **\n\n**Meet up Point:** Algonquin Park - Maggie Lake Entrance\n**Two Days
 ...sat and sun**\n**Fee for Trekking Training: $99.**\n\nBecause it was so
  much fun\, we are offering Trekker Training again in June!\nWe want you (
 and all our members) out Trekking. Don't give up your Sunday hikes\, but h
 ey it's time to up your hiking game!\nWhich is why we are offering skills 
 training for future trekkers so they can join in on trekking adventures ou
 tside of Ontario.\nThere is a lot to learn to prepare for a multi day trek
 k\, and we want you to be prepared. It is not just knowing what equipment 
 to buy\, how much to carry\, tent set up\, it's also food prep\, attitude\
 , and emergency skills and so much more!\nSo\, in order for you to ensure 
 you have a safe and the very BEST trekking experience we are offering an o
 vernight training experience.\n**Experienced Boots Trekkers feel free to h
 op in and show them how it's done!**\nWe will cover in one weekend -\n\n* 
 your weighted pack\n* pack pacing\n* water filtering\n* trail etiquette\n*
  safety\n* equipment must haves\n* first aid\n* atittude adjustment\n* fir
 e starting\n* navigation\n* ...and more
